IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 14 -- Transitional provisions (ss 53 to 58).
-- The commencement of each section is not stated in the text, so each commencement day is an input.

§ `Part 14 -- Transitional provisions`

§§ `Division 1 -- s 53`

-- src:1034 | (1) This section applies in relation to a Bill introduced in the Legislative Assembly before the commencement of this section.
@ref s 53(1) (src:1034-1034)
GIVEN `the Bill was introduced in the Legislative Assembly before the commencement of s 53` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53 applies in relation to the Bill (s 53(1))` IS
    IF `the Bill was introduced in the Legislative Assembly before the commencement of s 53` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Speech made to the Legislative Assembly` IS ONE OF
    `the speech made by the member when introducing the Bill`
    `the speech made by the member in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time`

-- src:1035 | (2) A reference in section 14B(3), definition extrinsic material, paragraph (f) to a speech made to the Legislative Assembly by the member when introducing the Bill is taken to be a reference to a speech made to the Legislative Assembly by the member in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time.
@ref s 53(2) (src:1035-1035)
GIVEN `s 53 applies in relation to the Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Speech made to the Legislative Assembly`
DECIDE `the speech that a reference in s 14B(3), definition extrinsic material, paragraph (f) is taken to be a reference to (s 53(2))` IS
    IF `s 53 applies in relation to the Bill`
    THEN JUST `the speech made by the member in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Division 2 -- ss 54 to 57`

-- src:1038 | In this division—
-- src:1039 | commencement means the commencement of this section.
@ref s 54 (src:1038-1039)
GIVEN `it is the commencement of s 54` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commencement in div 2 means the commencement of s 54 (s 54, definition commencement)` IS
    JUST `it is the commencement of s 54`

-- src:1040 | subordinate legislation does not include exempt subordinate legislation.
@ref s 54 (src:1040-1040)
GIVEN `it is exempt subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the legislation is subordinate legislation in div 2 (s 54, definition subordinate legislation)` IS
    IF `it is exempt subordinate legislation` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Section a reference is to` IS ONE OF
    `section 36`
    `section 48A`
    `section 49`
    `another section`

DECLARE `What a reference is taken to be` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to section 36 including a reference to schedule 1`
    `a reference to section 49`
    `a reference to section 48A`

-- s 55: references made before the commencement in an instrument; if the context permits, from the commencement
-- (a) a reference to s 36 includes schedule 1; (b) a reference to s 48A is taken to be a reference to s 49; (c) a reference to s 49 is taken to be a reference to s 48A.
-- src:1042 | (1) This section applies to references made before the commencement in an instrument.
@ref s 55(1) (src:1042-1042)
-- src:1043 | (2) If the context permits, from the commencement—
-- src:1044 | (a) a reference to section 36 of this Act is taken to include a reference to schedule 1 of this Act; and
-- src:1045 | (b) a reference to section 48A of this Act is taken to be a reference to section 49 of this Act; and
-- src:1046 | (c) a reference to section 49 of this Act is taken to be a reference to section 48A of this Act.
@ref s 55(2) (src:1043-1046)
GIVEN section IS A `Section a reference is to`
      `the reference was made before the commencement in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day of the commencement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a reference is taken to be`
DECIDE `what the reference is taken to be (s 55)` IS
    IF `the reference was made before the commencement in an instrument` AND `the context permits` AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day of the commencement`
    THEN CONSIDER section
        WHEN `section 36` THEN JUST `a reference to section 36 including a reference to schedule 1`
        WHEN `section 48A` THEN JUST `a reference to section 49`
        WHEN `section 49` THEN JUST `a reference to section 48A`
        WHEN `another section` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What gazetted or notified in the gazette is taken to refer to` IS ONE OF
    `notified or published in the gazette`
    `notified in the gazette under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47 as in force before the commencement`
    `notified under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47`

-- src:1048 | In an instrument, a reference to gazetted in relation to subordinate legislation is taken to be a reference to—
-- src:1049 | (a) for subordinate legislation notified or published in the gazette before the commencement—notified or published in the gazette; or
-- src:1050 | (b) otherwise—notified under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47.
@ref s 56 (src:1048-1050)
GIVEN `the subordinate legislation was notified or published in the gazette before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What gazetted or notified in the gazette is taken to refer to`
DECIDE `what a reference to gazetted is taken to be a reference to (s 56)` IS
    IF `the subordinate legislation was notified or published in the gazette before the commencement`
    THEN `notified or published in the gazette`
    ELSE `notified under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47`

-- src:1052 | In an instrument, a reference to notified in the gazette in relation to subordinate legislation is taken to be a reference to—
-- src:1053 | (a) for subordinate legislation notified in the gazette before the commencement—notified in the gazette under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47 as in force before the commencement; or
-- src:1054 | (b) otherwise—notified under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47.
@ref s 57 (src:1052-1054)
GIVEN `the subordinate legislation was notified in the gazette before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What gazetted or notified in the gazette is taken to refer to`
DECIDE `what a reference to notified in the gazette is taken to be a reference to (s 57)` IS
    IF `the subordinate legislation was notified in the gazette before the commencement`
    THEN `notified in the gazette under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47 as in force before the commencement`
    ELSE `notified under the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 47`

§§ `Division 3 -- s 58`

-- src:1057 | (1) This section applies if before the commencement—
-- src:1058 | (a) a form was approved or made available by an entity under an authorising law; and
-- src:1059 | (b) there had been no notification of the approval or availability of the form under previous section 48(5).
@ref s 58(1) (src:1057-1059)
GIVEN `before the commencement a form was approved or made available by an entity under an authorising law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there had been no notification of the approval or availability of the form under previous section 48(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 58 applies (s 58(1))` IS
    IF `before the commencement a form was approved or made available by an entity under an authorising law` AND `there had been no notification of the approval or availability of the form under previous section 48(5)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1060 | (2) On or after the day of commencement, the entity may notify the approval or availability of the form under amended section 48.
@ref s 58(2) (src:1060-1060)
GIVEN `s 58 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity may notify the approval or availability of the form under amended section 48 (s 58(2))` IS
    IF `s 58 applies` AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day of commencement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1061 | (3) In this section—
-- src:1062 | amended section 48 means section 48 as in force after the commencement.
@ref s 58(3), definition amended section 48 (src:1061-1062)
GIVEN `it is section 48 as in force after the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section is amended section 48 (s 58(3), definition amended section 48)` IS
    JUST `it is section 48 as in force after the commencement`

-- src:1063 | authorising law see section 48(1).
@ref s 58(3), definition authorising law (src:1063-1063)
GIVEN `it is the authorising law of s 48(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is the authorising law (s 58(3), definition authorising law)` IS
    JUST `it is the authorising law of s 48(1)`

-- src:1064 | form includes a new version of a form.
@ref s 58(3), definition form (src:1064-1064)
GIVEN `it is a new version of a form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new version is a form in s 58 (s 58(3), definition form)` IS
    IF `it is a new version of a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1065 | previous section 48(5) means section 48(5) as in force immediately before the commencement.
@ref s 58(3), definition previous section 48(5) (src:1065-1065)
GIVEN `it is section 48(5) as in force immediately before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subsection is previous section 48(5) (s 58(3), definition previous section 48(5))` IS
    JUST `it is section 48(5) as in force immediately before the commencement`
